# Data Storage Convention (Market Data)

## General Principles

- Organize data by business domain, not by sector or use case.
- Sector, industry, exchange, and company information must be stored as metadata, not encoded into folder structures.
- Folder names use lowercase and kebab-case.
- File names use lowercase and kebab-case, except ticker symbols which always preserve their official uppercase format.
- Store datasets in Apache Parquet unless another format is explicitly required.

## Directory Structure

```text
stock-data/
├── metadata/
│   ├── symbols.parquet
│   ├── companies.parquet
│   ├── exchanges.parquet
│   ├── sectors.parquet
│   ├── industries.parquet
│   └── trading-calendar.parquet
│
├── eod/
│   ├── hose/
│   │   ├── HPG.parquet
│   │   ├── FPT.parquet
│   │   └── ...
│   ├── hnx/
│   ├── upcom/
│   └── index/
│
├── intraday/
├── financials/
├── fundamentals/
├── corporate-actions/
├── ownership/
├── news/
├── macro/
├── derivatives/
├── warrants/
├── etf/
├── screener/
├── cache/
└── temp/
```

## EOD Storage

Each ticker owns one Parquet file containing its complete historical daily data.

Example:

```text
stock-data/eod/hose/HPG.parquet
stock-data/eod/hnx/SHS.parquet
```

Schema example:

```
date
open
high
low
close
volume
value
adjusted_close
...
```

## Financial Data

Financial statements are grouped by ticker.

```text
financials/
    HPG/
        income-statement.parquet
        balance-sheet.parquet
        cash-flow.parquet
        ratios.parquet
```

## Metadata

Metadata should contain all lookup information.

Examples:

- symbol
- exchange
- company
- sector
- industry
- isin
- listing_date
- status

Application code should always resolve metadata first before loading market data.

## Naming Rules

Folders

- lowercase
- kebab-case

Examples:

```
corporate-actions
trading-calendar
major-shareholder
```

Files

- lowercase
- kebab-case

Examples:

```
income-statement.parquet
balance-sheet.parquet
cash-flow.parquet
symbols.parquet
```

Ticker files

- Keep official ticker casing.

Examples:

```
HPG.parquet
FPT.parquet
VCI.parquet
VNINDEX.parquet
```

## Design Philosophy

- Organize by business domain.
- Never organize market data by sector.
- Metadata drives relationships.
- One ticker = one data file.
- Prefer immutable historical datasets.
- Keep directory structures stable as new data sources are added.